     "feedback": "Letter 20 (c. 829/1426) tells Shāhrukh that your aim in serving the Sharīʿa is to be blameless before the Prophet and to further his own mission, says you sent a dervish to court, and sends a treatise on the occult properties of things. Melvin-Koushki thinks that treatise was most probably the Suʾl al-Mulūk, because it carries the prediction about the Shahrukhid state; that identification is an inference, not a document."
