     "feedback": "Letter 27 (c. 830/1427, Herat?) is in your collection, so this is what you did; it is the same letter the recall scene cites, and here the game asks only whom you turn to first. It is a supplicant's letter: it shows what you asked of an amir, not what you held. Melvin-Koushki's footnote leaves open whether Fīrūzshāh had already ordered some of your property restored or was being asked to, and the pages give no reply and do not say whether the stipend was ever paid."
