     "evidence": "EV-0299",
     "kind": "apology",
     "direction": "supports",
     "reading": "Even in Nafsat I the argument runs that the Prophet bequeathed two kinds of knowledge, the more precious hidden. Melvin-Koushki reads the second subsection as heading toward the inner prophetic knowledge his own project claims; the game adds that this is an apology, so it shows what he told Shāhrukh.",
