     "reading": "The catalogue entry says the Tamhīd refers the reader to the Mafāḥiṣ, while Melvin-Koushki's own note calls it 'bare' of lettrist reference. If it points onward to the lettrist summa, the Tamhīd is less separable from the project than D needs it to be.",
