     "kind": "creed_tract",
     "direction": "strains",
     "reading": "The Iʿtiqādāt presents him as a staunch Sunni-Ashʿarī opposed to Muʿtazilism, philosophy, Shiʿism and messianic Sufism. Melvin-Koushki reads the apologies' self-portrait as 'a self-misrepresentation so exaggerated as to be cartoonish' and as shaped to Shāhrukh's programme; but it stands against the imamophile.",
