   "content": "Melvin-Koushki notes that the verse pretext is not explicitly mentioned in the first apology, which is primarily concerned with the charge of ṣūfīgarī; but the apology's sweeping dismissal of all but the Sunni confessional position and its heavy emphasis on Sufism as a purely Sunni phenomenon clearly imply that his Sunni credentials had also been questioned.",
