   "content": "In Nafsat I, per Melvin-Koushki, Ibn Turka says it is no small part of the glory of the Timurid state that it has done away with such perversions, but it is worth reminding the king to forestall their return, and lazy anarchists and cunning impostors are far from true Sufis and give the great masters a bad name.",
