   "content": "Melvin-Koushki says Ibn Turka fully accepts the validity of lettrism as occult praxis (his master Ḥusayn Akhlāṭī was renowned as a magus), but prefers to emphasize its neglected yet more important function as the basis for a broader occult philosophy.",
