   "content": "In the Prologue Melvin-Koushki says Ibn Turka's own prologue to the Mafāḥiṣ refuses the standard self-deprecation of author-as-wretch, dismisses all sources save two, thanks to his mentor Akhlāṭī, declines to give a book plan, and has no closing prayer.",
