     "reading": "Melvin-Koushki notes that the Tamhīd is bare of any reference to the author's central lettrist concerns. A modern reputation built on this one work is a reputation built on what he did not care about most. The catalogue entry for the Tamhīd (EV-0671) says it refers the reader to the Mafāḥiṣ; the two statements are Melvin-Koushki's own and have not been reconciled.",
