     "cites": [
      "REC-0052"
     ],
     "note": "Their ground is the Tamhīd, a staple Imami seminary text; Ṭabāṭabāʾī ranks him with Fārābī and Suhravardī in al-Mīzān, and Āshtiyānī and Javādī Āmulī treat the Tamhīd as definitive. Melvin-Koushki calls the image distorted and says the man himself would find the label cringe-inducing."
